  "description": "The Kegety is shaped by the textures of real terrain - gravel that shifts under load, dust, weather, and distance. Its geometry gives control and clean forward motion, creating a bike that feels planted and intuitive as the surface changes beneath it.\n\nKegety is a capable gravel bike that keeps going where the road ends. It is designed for speed and confidence when the surface becomes unpredictable. It is built for gravel racing, adventures and rides that link road, dirt and rough tracks into one route. The geometry is composed without feeling dull, giving stability when loaded or moving fast over broken ground.\n\nPaired with the ENVE Gravel In-Route fork, Kegety has generous tyre clearance to take on rougher roads and whatever lies beyond the tarmac.\n\nKegety is made for riders who push beyond neat categories. Gravel races, long mixed-surface days, loaded routes and fast exploration all ask different things of a bike. The frame balances clearance, stability and comfort so the bike remains calm when the terrain is not.\n\nLow-profile mudguard mounts are integrated into the frame and fork for year-round practicality without cluttering the frame. Use them when the forecast demands it. Forget they are there when it does not.\n\nKegety is designed around a dedicated 1x drivetrain layout. That allows us to optimise tyre clearance, simplify the frame and keep the bike focused on the demands of modern gravel riding. It is cleaner, more robust and better suited to the way this bike is intended to be used.\n\nWhat distinguishes the Kegety is its quiet assurance. The design concentrates on essentials and resolves them carefully, resulting in a bike that feels cohesive and enduring. It is a machine meant to disappear beneath the rider, leaving only the rhythm of the ride and the landscape ahead.",
